    "text": {
     "en": "Deserts are dry areas with very little rain, such as the Thar. Days are hot and nights are cold. Plants like cactus and animals like camels have special features.\nPeople adapt to their landforms. In mountains they build sloping roofs and terrace farms. On plains they grow crops and build cities. In deserts they use camels and store water.\nLandforms shape food, clothes, homes and work."
    }
